Package: unimlsurv
Type: Package
Title: Survival Analysis Modelling with 'mlr3'
Version: 0.2.2
Authors@R: person("Steve", "Shi", email = "19943405117@163.com", role =
        c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Steve Shi [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Steve Shi <19943405117@163.com>
Description: A time-to-event counterpart to 'uniml' with the same
        layering and the same objects. Survival outcomes are modelled
        with the 'mlr3' stack, imputation, scaling, and encoding are
        fitted on the training data only, and the reported statistics
        are the ones the survival literature actually defines:
        Harrell's concordance index, the
        inverse-probability-of-censoring weighted Brier score of Graf
        and colleagues, the integrated Brier score, the
        cumulative/dynamic time-dependent area under the ROC curve,
        time-point calibration against Kaplan-Meier estimates, and
        time-point decision-curve analysis. All time points are chosen
        by the user.
